        "@type": "HowToStep",
        "text": "To remove the excess salt from the fish, first rinse under running water, then soak several hours or overnight in water. Alternatively, or in addition, place rinsed and soaked salted fish in a deep pot of water filled halfway (to prevent overflowing), over medium flame, and boil for 10-15 minutes. Drain, rinse with clean running water, press out excess water using your hands or a strainer and flake with a fork or your fingers. [After draining, I always test the saltiness of the fish. I may rinse or boil again depending on the result.] You do not want to remove all the salt from the fish and you do not want excess water(moisture)."
